## 4. Exact closure optimum (all monomial sets in the bounding box)

Box support (Newton polytope `[0,d]^m`, verified in §2), every vertex class `a = d·1_S`, `|S| = s`. 
Bounding box `[0,L]^m`. `best box ≤ L` = max over `L' ≤ L` of the box strategy `M = [0,L']^m` (closed form); 
`bounded` = that best box is `[0,L]^m` itself (the optimum would grow with a larger bounding box). 
`Σk ≤ charge` is the machine check of the 1/(md) argument on the optimum.

